{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 37, :comments ["<b>Deeper than the skin.</b> This word has no sister-word, and we cannot know whether it is a quadriliteral doubled in its final letter, or a five-letter word. According to the sense of the context, some say it means like marks or threads. Others say it is a compound word, from the sense of ותשקע האש (and the fire sinks down), and ורורות from the root רר as in בשרו (his flesh) — but this is far-fetched." "<b>And their appearance.</b> The appearance of each one of them is low."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {0 "The lemma שקערורות (Lev. 14:37) describes plague marks 'deeper than the skin'; the exact parsing of the word is disputed and rendered here according to the context."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:10:11.269016861Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}